# Working title: "Defuse Craft" (CS2 rules + maps inside Minecraft: Java)

Paste this whole file to an agent running on your PC (Claude Code or Codex) that has your Melty connection. The Melty and universal-modder instructions you pasted earlier still apply; this file answers all the design questions so the agent should not ask any more.

## 1. Design decisions (locked)
- Mode: single player vs bots. No multiplayer, so no recipe.multiplayer.
- Primary game (role "primary"): Minecraft: Java Edition, Fabric via portable Prism Launcher instance, as in SkyCraft (mashup_info skycraft).
- Companion game (role "companion"): Counter-Strike 2, never launched, never modded, never copied. Its folder comes in as {game:counter-strike-2}.
- Bodies and combat: Minecraft skins and Minecraft melee/bow combat. No CS2 agents or guns.
- CS2 brings: (a) one map layout, (b) rules, (c) sounds and music. Maps and audio are read at runtime from the player's own CS2 install.
- First version: one map, one bomb site, first to 4 rounds, 5v5 (player + 4 bot teammates vs 5 bots).
- License: MIT. Remixing allowed. Credit: Melty account name.
- Do not ship any CS2 or Minecraft assets. Ship only the mod jar, config and the bundled libraries whose licenses allow it.

## 2. Listing draft (adjust after the real build exists)
- Title: Defuse Craft
- Tagline: Plant and defuse the bomb on a CS2 map rebuilt in Minecraft blocks, with Minecraft swords and bows.
- Description: Play a bomb-defusal match against bots as a normal Minecraft character. A buy phase lets you spend round money on Minecraft gear, then you fight over a bomb site on a CS2 layout rebuilt from your own Counter-Strike 2 install, with CS2's sound effects and round music. Requires Minecraft: Java Edition and Counter-Strike 2.

